  "scope_assessment": [
    "The accepted legacy_archive_inventory maps to exactly 20 linked table rows: norm_bounding 3, FjORD 8, FL-MAML 5, CS-MAML 4. Each retained path, exact source hash, family, filename label and descriptive role matches the author receipt and accepted inventory.",
    "The public text distinguishes entrypoints, trainer/server/client helpers, model definitions and TOML configurations. Dataset/Gym utilities are described separately and do not become maintained experiment entrypoints.",
    "Dependencies are tied to preserved source imports and TOML selections. No complete historical environment or version pin is invented. The page makes no historical execution or successful restoration claim.",
    "The four estimates are explicitly preliminary planning ranges for bounded implementation/review fixtures. Environment recovery, research semantics, external assets and paper-scale results may add work; FjORD ViT remains separate and CS-MAML depends on FL-MAML work.",
    "Norm bounding preserves the valid aggregate_deltas override hook and describes the actual None fallback, direct NumPy conversion and unweighted clipped sum. Numerical, device and research-semantic validation remain future work.",
    "FjORD eagerly imports its local ResNet and Torch/einops ViT modules. Its ptflops import, disabled resource-limit TOML branch, size comparison against both limits and subtotal aggregation code support the qualified restoration questions. No retired legacy-factory dependency is claimed.",
    "FL-MAML reads optimizer fields from a different section than its supplied TOML, references undefined optimizers/lr_scheduler names in scheduler branches and supplies 9 positional arguments to each stage call requiring 10. Its inner/outer gradient semantics are explicitly unqualified.",
    "CS-MAML has a working-directory-relative sibling FL-MAML import and central/edge personalization event paths. Its four positional server.run arguments match the current base signature. That match is appropriately separated from real cross-silo qualification.",
    "Existing modern retirement/provenance content and the accepted deployment/source base are preserved. This prose review adds no active-family, packaging, global repository qualification or published-PR integration claim."
  ],
